  "hints": [
    "Row n (0-indexed) has n + 1 entries starting and ending with 1.",
    "Each next binomial coefficient follows C(n, k+1) = C(n, k) * (n - k) // (k + 1), or build rows iteratively from [1].",
    "Pseudocode:\n  row = [1]\n  for k in range(n):\n      row.append(row[-1] * (n - k) // (k + 1))\n  return row"
